Subject: [PATCH 02281/11362] [outer-loop] gap-fill findings: loop is sound,
 but a heuristic needs the RIGHT engine (v3 can't solve cn04 regardless)

Validated with a PERFECT deterministic diff-from-win heuristic: graph_explore_solve_v3
does NOT solve cn04 with OR without it (novelty-only also fails), while v2 solves cn04.
So cn04-in-v3 was the wrong test -- the heuristic was doomed by the engine, not the LLM.
A goal-distance heuristic's value is EFFICIENCY in a search that already reaches the win
(lp85 OfflineSolver+hand_verifier = 10.75x). Next: target lp85 / make v2 heuristic-guided.
Autolearning capture-and-reuse + the runtime validator are built and correct (they refused
every broken heuristic). Local models (12B AND 35B) write None-falling heuristics -> hard
float-return contract is the prompt fix (size-independent).

